WEBVTT

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.270
Adolescence Points

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:04.020
Let's talk about the "Adolescence Points."

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.610
These points are earned when one has an adolescent-like experience.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:13.590
Activities can award a maximum of 5 points.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:17.160
Let's take a look at all of the activities, starting with: +1.

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:20.950
These activities include things like
talking to girls during lunch break...

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.040
...and eating out with friends on the way home from school.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:29.630
They're pretty much just points that get added up as one goes through the school day.

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.590
However, if the adolescence points are left alone,

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:34.630
they will decrease with each passing day.

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:37.260
These activities may have been enjoyable at the time,

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.180
but in hindsight, they weren't all that memorable.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.230
However, due to the risks of regretting it later,

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.890
no-one should sit in their comfort zone and do nothing.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.190
Next: +2.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:53.400
A good example would be talking with a girl who is around the same age at night in the park.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.820
When an activity normally getting a +1 meets certain conditions,

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:59.700
such as "at night" or"during club events", an extra point is added.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:00.700
+1 is given to basic activities,

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.620
so the +2 is a sign of how they happened.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.500
For individuals blessed with both talent and good looks...

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.630
...it's possible to earn up to 20 points
during their three years of high school.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:16.630
These points may not help with enrolling in a good university or getting a job,

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.640
but when an average person is on the verge of death,

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.640
the satisfaction gained from these points can
mean the difference between Heaven and Hell.

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:26.140
In the end, people live for the sake of that moment, after all.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:30.150
Do you now understand just how important high school life is?

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:35.650
Well, I'm just trying to improvise a bit and define it, because I'm bored, though...

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:31.900
TL Note: Makoto is trying to write "青春ポイント;Adolescence Points" here

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.920
ni-nensei baka wa hitori

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.920
２年生 バカは一人

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.920
2nd year of high school, there is an idiot,

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.970
koko no machi no sora miageru

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.970
ここの町の 空見上げる

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.970
Looking up into space from this.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.640
sabori gakusei pajama kiteru

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.640
サボり学生 パジャマ着てる

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.640
A truant student wearing pyjamas,

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.060
natsuyasumi ga kozu ni chuutai

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.060
夏休みが 来ずに中退

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.060
Not waiting for summer break, the student quits school.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:09.650
chikyuu de uchuujin nante adana demo

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:09.650
地球で宇宙人なんてあだ名でも

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:09.650
Even being nicknamed an alien on Earth,

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:20.450
uchuu no machiawase shitsu ni wa motto hen na anata ga ita no

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:20.450
宇宙の待ち合わせ室にはもっと変なあなたがいたの

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:20.450
in the waiting room in space, an even weirder you was there.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:27.200
jushin shiteru kana to setsuzoku shite miru to

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:27.200
受信してるかなと 接続してみると

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:27.200
I wonder if you are receiving this; I thought I'd try connecting.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:34.090
minna ga sakeru naka de pachikuri miteiru anata ga ita kara

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:34.090
みんなが避ける中で ぱちくり見ているあなたがいたから

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:34.090
Because while everyone else was avoiding it, you were there watching.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:40.890
telepathy kimochi ga denpa ga chigakutemo

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:40.890
テレパシ気持ちが 電波が違くても

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:40.890
Even if these feelings I am transmitting
telepathically are the wrong wavelength,

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:44.220
kitto ne nanika tsukande kureteru

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:44.220
きっとね 何か掴んでくれてる

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:44.220
I'm sure you will catch something.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:47.640
anata no koto ga suki

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:47.640
あなたのことが好き

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:47.640
I love you.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:03:01.110
jushin shite kureru no kana to, shinpai mo shiterun desu

00:02:53.690 --> 00:03:01.110
受信してくれるのかなと心配もしてるんです

00:02:53.690 --> 00:03:01.110
I wonder if you will receive this from me; I'm starting to worry.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.450
nandakanda de soba ni ite kureteru

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.450
なんだかんだで側にいてくれてる

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.450
You're with me no matter what happens.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:07.240
anata ga suki

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:07.240
あなたが好き

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:07.240
I love you.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:12.250
kitto anata shika jushin dekinai no

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:12.250
きっとあなたしか受信できないの?

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:12.250
I'm sure you are the only person that can receive this.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.210
I can't...

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:19.670
...fly!

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:27.060
I got a +5!

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:27.060
In exchange for the points, I was hospitalised.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:38.090
Upon hitting the ocean's surface, my arm snapped from the impact.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:41.110
Furthermore, the fracture was quite severe.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.070
I had a hard time swimming back to the shore.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:51.580
With Erio, too, it was a miracle we didn't drown.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:56.920
The pain in my arm was so fierce that I even felt like crying.

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:01.760
The spring sea was a lot colder than I had expected.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.260
The bicycle still sits at the bottom of the sea.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.460
I lost my ability to go to school, while Erio...

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:12.180
...lost the sliver of hope she held so dear.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:18.220
I wanted to ask myself, "Was there any point to this?"

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:21.640
Instead, a feeling more like guilt tugged at my heart.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:24.550
As children grow up,

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:27.400
they can just learn for themselves that Santa doesn't exist.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.080
But sometimes adults will cruelly tell them so.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:32.580
Feeling as if I'd done just that, I began to question myself.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.830
After getting out of the sea, we didn't exchange any words as we walked.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:40.300
In the end, we even let go of each other's hands.

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:43.800
Hm?

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:55.560
Niwa-ku~n!

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.060
This is a delusion.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:03.570
Transfer Student...

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.070
This is also a delusion.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.750
Mako-kun, you're late.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.080
It's nappy time!

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.080
Nappy time!

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.580
"This is also a delusion."

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.210
Come on.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:17.210
Well, that's what I'd like to think.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.330
Come on. Come on.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:22.040
I'll leave your change of clothes here.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:26.220
Then, there's your allowance, and I brought some stewed porridge.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:27.400
Meme-san.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:28.600
What is it?

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:30.530
Did Erio say anything?

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:31.840
What do you mean?

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.300
Let's see.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.230
Nothing in particular.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:37.900
I wonder how Meme-san feels.

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:40.520
When she found us drenched and rushed us to the hospital,

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:43.400
she didn't get angry or scold us at all.

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:44.930
She didn't say a word.

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:47.530
She seemed indifferent as she
handled the hospitalisation procedures.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:48.550
Hey, Mako-kun.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:49.510
Yes?

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:51.010
A long, long time ago,

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:53.850
in a certain place, there once lived a man and a woman.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.910
The man... Well, who cares about him?

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:59.970
The woman, who even now has such delicate, peachy, fine skin,

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:03.950
lives with a young man named Mako-kun who makes her sore night after night.

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:05.210
Hey! Don't say any more, you idiot!

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:06.470
What's this, all of a sudden?

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:08.650
You seem to have trouble falling asleep,

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:11.230
so I thought I'd chat with you.

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:13.210
Did you want a goodnight kiss instead?

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:14.220
Or even better, chuu~

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:17.520
I feel like I'd end up having a nightmare, so I'll pass.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.070
Is the man Erio's father?

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:22.200
Yes, a foreigner named Elliot.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.290
Erio and husband, so his name is Elliot.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.290
TL Note: "husband" is pronounced as "oto" here, so Erio + oto = Elliot.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:27.440
Yeah, right. You've already had the name set.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:30.440
Yes, I went <i>pe pe pe</i> on a calculator.

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:32.850
A father who comes out of a calculator...

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:39.150
He was such a cool person.

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:40.420
Even if he would have lived with us,

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.460
I don't think it would've worked out.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:49.800
We broke up because we had different
personal values or something? So everything turned out for the best.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:53.260
There are moments when being a single parent can be difficult, but...

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:55.150
Well, whatever!

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:57.250
Mako-kun is here with us now.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:00.570
You're a bit young to be a substitute husband, though.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:03.300
What's wrong?

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:06.100
I-I have a bit of a fever.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:08.740
Huh? Are you okay?

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.910
I-I can't gain any points from this.

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:13.370
In a way, I'm just setting up myself for deductions.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.050
See you, Mako-kun.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:28.880
I feel like my adolescence would be over if I got too involved with that person.

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:36.010
I wonder how many points I'm at right now.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:38.600
I've only been keeping track of it when I feel like it, using simple arithmetic.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:41.070
To be honest, I don't really have a clear idea.

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:44.860
The kind of events that give more than +2 adolescence points...

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.250
is subjective and varies based on the individual.

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:52.030
The easiest example of a +3 and higher case would be a date with one's crush,

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:54.950
but that only applies if the two aren't dating, or if it's an unrequited love.

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:59.290
There are also other special cases for large group events.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:02.870
Since cultural festivals and other similar activities rarely occur,

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:05.510
they can often award up to +4 points.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:11.630
Lastly, based on the individual's own values, an activity that stands out and achieves a reaction of, "This is it!"..

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:14.720
...would be that person's very own +5.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:18.970
Only those individuals who have run around town, oblivious to everything else, for the sake of someone of the opposite sex,

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:21.980
struggled for victory at the high school baseball nationals,

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:26.150
or have stepped over the boundaries of trauma and glory and kept on going at full-sprint...

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:29.320
...have the right to earn the maximum addition of +5.

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:34.490
She probably won't come to visit me.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:37.380
I have no reason to think that, but somehow, I just feel that way.

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:41.170
Ah... it itches.

00:08:45.030 --> 00:08:46.920
Mako-chan, morning!

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:50.630
Ah, was I being a bit too intimate?

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:52.630
Not at all. It's okay.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:54.290
If a certain Auntie had said that,

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:56.010
I would've told her, "Yes. Never call me that again."

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:59.480
Oh, right.

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:01.890
What's the matter?

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:06.790
My hair is a mess, and it's embarrassing.

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:10.960
The wind was like "Fuwa!" so I was like "Dokusha!" with my helmet,

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:13.500
so then my sweat was like "Mechua!" you see.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:16.310
I tried my best to tidy it,

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:18.740
but I just couldn't get it to fluff up.

00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:19.930
Is it weird?

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:21.740
This is a boy's hat...

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:22.810
Extremely.

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:24.700
You could be mistaken for a boy.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:25.790
Huh? Really?

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:27.960
Can I punch you?

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:32.300
Her clenched fist looks as frightening as a child's.

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:34.670
She's so cute.

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:35.550
Huh?

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:36.470
Ah...

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:39.140
I'm not cute!

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:40.930
Not at all!

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:42.720
I'm just a plain girl.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:47.050
I got rejected by two boys during my first year, after all.

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:47.630
Sorry.

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:48.430
Did I creep you out?

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:50.480
Y-Yes! A lot!

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:51.910
I'm sorry.

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:52.860
Never mind.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:55.650
Actually, not really, now that I take a closer look.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:57.740
If you saw me from far away, would you think I was a stalker or something?

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:02.030
May I start over from the beginning?

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:03.540
You may.

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:04.750
Well, then...

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:08.420
Here's a copy of the notes.

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:10.420
The midterms are coming up after all.

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:12.350
Wow, thank you!

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:16.860
If there's anything you don't understand, feel free to ask me for help.

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:18.420
I'm not a prodigy or anything,

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:21.050
so I don't know if I'll be of much help, though.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:22.210
Not at all.

00:10:22.210 --> 00:10:24.320
You're the only one I can depend on, Sensei.

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:25.560
No, not at all.

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:29.340
Say...

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:34.440
You didn't jump into the ocean because you were trying to commit suicide, did you?

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.260
Ah, I see.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:38.570
She's heard about what I did.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:43.130
No, that wasn't why at all.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:44.240
I see.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:47.870
Though, when I was falling, I really thought I was going to die.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:49.510
It's not good to die!

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:50.570
Never!

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:54.040
Um, the person may be personally fine with it,

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:57.330
but the people who are left behind would be distressed for sure.

00:10:57.330 --> 00:11:01.890
Furthermore, people who think "No one cares" and look down on themselves are the worst.

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:03.600
Yeah.

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:05.220
I'm sure you'd have been sad, too, Ryuushi-san.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:07.220
I told you, it's Ryuuko!

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:11.780
I bet you could get the whole school to cry for you, Niwa-kun.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:15.540
I'd believe it if it were the other extreme.

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:17.570
That wouldn't happen!

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:20.340
I'd keep that extreme from happening

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:25.990
Transfer Student, have you been bored?

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:30.450
Huh? You guys aren't laughing.

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:32.440
It's a hospital, so I thought aubergine and nurse...

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:32.440
TL Note: "Aubergine" is pronounced "Nasu," while "Nurse" is "Naasu".

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:34.540
Please, you don't have to explain.

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:37.920
Maekawa-san, you were that kind of character?

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.050
Yeah.

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:41.310
Hey, Maekawa-san.

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:42.430
You're here to visit Niwa-kun?

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:43.320
Huh?

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:44.760
Ryuushi-san is being kind of scary.

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:46.850
Why else would I be here?

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.850
That one's scary, as well, though in a different way.

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:53.070
Since when did you two become so close?

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:55.860
You never talk to each other in class.

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:59.740
Since Transfer Student and I spent a night together, I guess.

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:02.610
H-Hey!

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:05.240
Jokes like that may end up ruining my imag-

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:08.740
See...

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:11.210
You said you spent a night together.

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:12.750
It's night! It's pitch black!

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:13.630
It's a false accusation.

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:14.670
No, it's completely made up!

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:17.520
As much as I'd love to have an experience like that, I didn't do it!

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:19.280
You'd love to?!

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:20.450
Hey Kibonengu.

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:24.120
Because of what you said, my high school life is being ruined!

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:26.970
I mean, I thought that if I added up all the time we spent at night,

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:29.350
it'd add up to about one full night.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:31.700
That isn't like adding points at a supermarket!

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:33.410
Don't add them up!

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:44.080
It seems like a refreshing breeze has blown through your boring and degenerating hospital life.

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:45.280
No, more like a hurricane...

00:12:45.810 --> 00:12:49.890
I didn't expect Ryuushi to give such a nice reaction.

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:51.120
Her love towards you must be quite strong.

00:12:51.550 --> 00:12:52.940
That's not true!

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:54.620
And my name isn't Ryuushi!

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:59.540
She'll be back soon, since all of her stuff is still here.

00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:00.920
Now, then.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:03.090
Excuse me for a moment...

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:10.180
It was so hot.

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:13.430
The school uniform cosplay suits you better.

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:14.930
This isn't a cosplay.

00:13:14.930 --> 00:13:16.940
It's my occupation.

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:20.690
Transfer Student, I heard you jumped into the ocean.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:24.720
Were you trying to turn into a fish or something?

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:27.700
No, I was trying to fly.

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:29.850
I didn't have enough propulsion, so I fell.

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:30.670
What?

00:13:30.670 --> 00:13:31.950
You were trying to become a bird instead, huh?

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.910
I wanted to fly even higher than that, perhaps.

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:40.040
Tell this to Touwa for me:

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:43.050
"We should dress up as Grays together sometime."

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:45.720
Were my actions that easy to read?

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:47.430
Maybe.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:49.430
Got it. I'll tell her.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:54.140
On another note, let's go to the beach together this summer.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:57.190
That really is on a completely different note, Onee-sama.

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:08.320
What are you doing?

00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:10.950
It's the season for shoulder charges.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:15.190
Pin Pon Pan Pon! The beach is off limits!

00:14:15.190 --> 00:14:15.910
Why?

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:17.160
Because there are jellyfish.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:18.370
Jellyfish?

00:14:18.910 --> 00:14:19.970
Yes.

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:22.950
So you're saying a boy and a girl

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:26.390
No, that I can't go to the beach with Niwa-kun.

00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:28.190
This has nothing to do with Niwa-kun!

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:29.250
A boy and girl at the beach!

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:31.020
It makes me shiver just thinking about it!

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:32.440
It's impure or whatever you call it.

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:35.110
What does that make Transfer Student, then?

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:37.180
He did more than just go to the beach.

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:40.020
He did something that indecent?

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:41.610
What? You didn't know?

00:14:43.090 --> 00:14:45.980
Transfer Student is Touwa's cousin.

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:48.370
Hey!

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:50.950
You were supposed to keep that a secret from everyone.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:53.890
Well, it's the truth, so there's nothing I can really say.

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:56.530
Even if we're estranged, it's easy to figure out.

00:14:56.530 --> 00:15:00.580
I'm just telling the truth, after all.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:03.630
This is the only way I can accept it.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:09.090
Actually, I'm living with Erio.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:11.970
What did you just say?!

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:13.170
Wait!

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:14.970
One of you knows that already.

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:20.390
My stay at the hospital ended after two weeks.

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:23.720
It was a weekday, and no one came to pick me up.

00:15:23.720 --> 00:15:25.220
If it had been on the weekend...

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:27.780
I shouldn't get carried away with my delusions.

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:31.090
Ryuushi-san said she doesn't mind that I'm Erio's cousin, but...

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:33.760
It was easy to tell from her awkwardness that she wasn't okay with it.

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:37.370
She's a person who can't help expressing all of her emotions openly.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:40.000
I'm sure any other person would say the same.

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:42.860
But even knowing that,

00:15:42.860 --> 00:15:46.350
it's impossible to completely understand a person's true intentions.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:50.960
A person's subconscious is like an extraterrestrial being.

00:15:51.610 --> 00:15:55.260
No one knows what it really is and can only catch glimpses of it.

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:59.070
The reason Erio wrapped herself in a futon...

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:02.090
Maybe she wanted to be like an alien, even if it was just on the surface,

00:16:02.090 --> 00:16:04.980
and after trial and error, that was the method she found.

00:16:05.630 --> 00:16:09.150
She wanted to be unidentified.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:18.910
I'm home.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:48.690
M-Mako-kun... It's c-cold...

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:49.680
I'm here.

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:51.940
Are you all right?

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:55.120
Mako-kun, warm me up with your body-

00:16:57.970 --> 00:16:58.870
Come on in.

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:01.330
I'm not sure I want to ask, but what are you doing?

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:03.720
I was cooling myself off.

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:05.460
Enough of this, already.

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:10.870
After I went to all the trouble of hiding in here for the past five minutes, Mako-kun is so cold.

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:13.920
I almost wanted to hang myself there for a moment.

00:17:15.270 --> 00:17:17.720
Here we go...

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:18.970
Okay!

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:21.310
To commemorate Mako-kun's release-

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:22.350
My discharge from the hospital.

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:23.600
Yes, yes. That.

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:25.870
Let's eat out for lunch.

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:27.560
It's just a family restaurant, though.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:29.400
That having been said, go get Erio.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:30.360
She's on the second floor.

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:31.730
Me?

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:35.550
In this house, that's Mako-kun's job.

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:52.550
Eri-

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:53.170
Oh?

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:56.590
I'm home!

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:01.510
H-He's here!

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:03.520
Rather, you should show yourself.

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:08.910
Is your arm all right?

00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:11.800
I'm fine, except that I want to scratch at it.

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:13.130
Sorry.

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:13.940
Once again,

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:18.080
Touwa Erio, 16 years old.

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:22.200
My occupation is... helping out with housework.

00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:24.250
Cousin is back.

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:25.710
Yeah.

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:28.290
Meme-san said that we're going out to eat.

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:29.420
Okay.

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:30.980
Take the futon off when we go.

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:36.260
I wonder if aliens exist.

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:37.360
I'm not sure.

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:41.930
I only proved that you're my shut-in cousin who helps with housework.

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:44.930
It feels like I'm being looked down upon.

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:47.680
It's like... How do I say this...

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:49.510
How do you say it?

00:18:49.510 --> 00:18:51.560
I'm sorry for destroying your dreams.

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:53.060
It's fine.

00:18:54.470 --> 00:18:57.210
Having amnesia was scary,

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:59.570
but thanks to Cousin, I was able to fly a little bit.

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:01.910
I feel a lot better now.

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:06.870
So, to show my gratitude...

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:13.450
There are still some electromagnetic waves left in you, huh?

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:17.390
Before, Cousin told mother that he wanted a girl's panties.

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:18.860
You were listening?

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:21.910
Aren't you able to assess whether something is a joke or not?

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:24.890
That was the conclusion I reached after much deliberation.

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:27.950
Ah, anyway,

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:30.910
there doesn't seem to be anything I can do about your amnesia.

00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:31.690
Sorry.

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:33.150
That's fine.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:35.070
I'll do something about it, myself.

00:19:36.630 --> 00:19:39.280
I shouldn't have quit school.

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:40.260
Yeah.

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:42.090
It helps when you want to find a job.

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:43.410
No, that's not it.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:46.160
Going to school with Cousin...

00:19:46.630 --> 00:19:48.270
...seems like it would be so much fun.

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:54.170
So slow!

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:55.410
I don't want to get a sunburn.

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:58.800
I wish you two would've come out faster.

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:00.740
Wait. All three of us are going to ride on this?

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:01.880
Don't worry.

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:04.770
Auntie is very light, just like driver paper!

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:06.950
I don't understand at all...

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:08.350
Who's steering?

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:10.070
Mako-kun, of course.

00:20:10.070 --> 00:20:11.910
I'll be riding in the back.

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:13.170
My, how bittersweet!

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:15.060
I'm injured, you know.

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:16.150
What about Erio?

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:17.420
Here.

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:19.780
This isn't supposed to be a stunt ride...

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:27.780
Don't hold on to me, please.

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:31.730
What percentage of that statement has to do with hiding your embarrassment?

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:33.710
About 0.03%.

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:35.170
What about for me?

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:40.180
About 5 centimetres per second!

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:40.180
TL Note: A reference to the anime film; 5 Centimetres Per Second, directed by Shinkai Makoto.

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:44.050
That day... The day we flew in the sky...

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:47.050
If the bike's speed hadn't suddenly increased...

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:50.560
...we wouldn't have gained enough distance, landing on the cliff's rocks.

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:54.890
Just how was that worn-out bike able to
suddenly fix itself right before we jumped?

00:20:55.390 --> 00:20:57.150
It's fine, even if was just a coincidence.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:59.980
But where are the aliens?

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:02.180
So long as that question mark is not removed,

00:21:02.180 --> 00:21:04.030
it's quite a valuable question.

00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:07.160
Touwa Erio is an Earthling.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:10.950
She's not a cyborg or anything, just someone with amnesia.

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:17.580
But if this person somehow really is an alien who oversees this town...

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:19.670
...she may be adored by everyone.

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:23.220
Gravity is the worst!

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:24.300
Agreed!

00:21:25.300 --> 00:21:28.290
This bicycle won't take flight today.

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:30.580
Instead, it will carry us, people who are not aliens,

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:33.030
to some place here on Earth.

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:37.980
What's that?

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:44.320
I'm aiming to be this store's mascot girl.

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:46.710
All right.

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:48.870
Maekawa-san. Go clean up out the front.

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:51.030
While looking like this?

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:53.250
While looking like that.

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:54.580
Aye aye, sir.

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:57.660
Huh?!

00:21:57.660 --> 00:21:58.830
You're really going to?

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:03.710
Hm?

00:22:08.480 --> 00:22:09.490
Huh?

00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:19.100
kaze hiku no, kaze hiku no

00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:19.100
風邪引くの 風邪引くの

00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:19.100
I'll catch a cold; I'll catch a cold.

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:23.020
ofuton nakute samui

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:23.020
おふとんなくて寒い

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:23.020
It's cold without a futon.

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:27.070
ofuton hagasarete samui

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:27.070
おふとんはがされて寒い

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:27.070
It's cold when the futon is pulled off.

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:31.990
yoake ni anata ga kuru

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:31.990
夜明けにあなたが来る

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:31.990
In the morning, you come.

00:22:31.990 --> 00:22:35.830
anata ga waratteiru

00:22:31.990 --> 00:22:35.830
あなたが笑っている

00:22:31.990 --> 00:22:35.830
You have a smile on your face.

00:22:36.660 --> 00:22:45.550
kitto boku ni wa mienai to omotteiru

00:22:36.660 --> 00:22:45.550
きっと僕には見えないと思っている

00:22:36.660 --> 00:22:45.550
You must think I can't see you.

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:49.930
sotto te wo nobashite

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:49.930
そっと手を伸ばして

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:49.930
You slowly extend your hand out.

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:54.970
ittai nani wo suru tsumori?

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:54.970
一体何をするつもり?

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:54.970
Just what are you trying to do?

00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:59.600
kaze hiku no, kaze hiku no

00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:59.600
風邪引くの　風邪引くの

00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:59.600
I'll catch a cold; I'll catch a cold.

00:23:01.860 --> 00:23:05.610
netafuri wo shite sugosu

00:23:01.860 --> 00:23:05.610
寝たふりをして過ごす

00:23:01.860 --> 00:23:05.610
I pretend that I am asleep.

00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:10.110
sukoshi dake atatakaku naru

00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:10.110
少しだけ暖かくなる

00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:10.110
It's become just a bit warmer.

00:23:10.700 --> 00:23:14.700
tonari de anata ga nemuru

00:23:10.700 --> 00:23:14.700
隣であなたが眠る

00:23:10.700 --> 00:23:14.700
You are sleeping next to me.

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:22.460
urusai negoto wa mushi shite

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:22.460
うるさい寝言は無視して

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:22.460
I ignore your annoying sleep talk.

00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:32.140
kasanaru odeko ni kisu shite

00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:32.140
重なるおでこにキスして

00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:32.140
I put my lips to your forehead and kiss it.

00:23:40.720 --> 00:23:42.660
Fracturing my right arm: -2

00:23:42.660 --> 00:23:44.400
Wanting to scratch at my right arm: -1

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:46.730
Meme-san was sleeping in my bed: -1

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:48.860
Ryuushi-san came to visit me: +2

00:23:48.860 --> 00:23:50.880
Nasukawa-san invaded: -1

00:23:50.880 --> 00:23:52.410
Home sweet home: +2

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:54.240
Erio smiled: +3

00:23:54.240 --> 00:23:58.080
Received a girl's panties: +... No, -1

